inux-x64-0.205.0.deb"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/releases/assets/448500210","id":448500210,"node_id":"RA_kwDOSbOoU84au5Hy","name":"formal-ai-desktop-linux-x64-0.205.0.tar.gz","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","rec…10028 tokens truncated…dbox (incl. an unrelated-context\n  negative): all pass.\n- `experiments/issue-395-cross-runtime-codegen-parity.mjs` — 170/170 cells\n  byte-identical (no regression).\n- `tests/integration/issue_412_oracle_languages.rs` + the\n  `source_tests/{knowledge,solver_handler_oracle}` suites — the coding oracle\n  (R6) and the bounded-cache ratchet (R8).\n- `experiments/issue-412-js-oracle.mjs` — the worker's oracle path, byte-identical\n  to the Rust `solve()` output.\n- Full suites green under `-Dwarnings`: `cargo test --test source` (387),\n  `--test unit` (814), `--test integration` (35), `cargo clippy --all-targets`;\n  total-closure audit 0 unresolved.\n\n## Repository-wide mandate (R6–R8)\n\nIssue #412 also demanded broad, repository-wide generalization, delivered **in\nthis PR** (not deferred):\n\n- **R6 — external knowledge bases as cached APIs.** `src/knowledge.rs` models\n  Rosetta Code / Wikifunctions / Hello World Collection / Stack Overflow as\n  external sources treated as APIs even though they expose none. The\n  `write_program` fallback (`src/solver_handler_oracle.rs`, mirrored in the\n  worker) answers languages the verified catalogue never templated\n  (Kotlin/Swift/PHP/Bash/Lua/Haskell hello-world + a Rosetta-Code Kotlin\n  factorial) from an embedded popular-case cache — snippet + deterministic\n  output + source attribution — while catalogued languages keep their verified\n  route. A gated live-refresh (the existing `FORMAL_AI_LIVE_API` discipline) is\n  what would materialise per-source `data/cache/<slug>/` buckets.\n- **R8 — bounded cache.** `cache_capacity` / `within_cache_capacity` /\n  `KNOWLEDGE_CACHE_FLOOR` enforce `min(1%, 512)` clamped to source size, with a\n  ratchet test that fails CI if the committed snapshot set exceeds the cap.\n- **R7 — meta-algorithm that builds algorithms.** The compositional foundation\n  ships (the numeric-list path builds programs by composing scaffolds + idioms\n  from `data/seed/coding-idioms.lino`, validated through the meta-language CST —\n  \"add an operation/language = add seed data, not code\"). Unifying the remaining\n  bespoke coding handlers under one task-agnostic composer is a larger\n  first-principles refactor; its status and the scoping question are tracked in\n  [`docs/case-studies/issue-412/README.md`](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/blob/issue-412-1f5f93827186/docs/case-studies/issue-412/README.md)\n  §7.4 and the PR thread.\n\nSee the deep case study under\n[`docs/case-studies/issue-412/`](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/blob/issue-412-1f5f93827186/docs/case-studies/issue-412/README.md)\nfor the full requirement-by-requirement breakdown (R1–R12) and online research.\n","headRefName":"issue-412-1f5f93827186","mergedAt":"2026-06-11T16:54:12Z","number":413,"title":"fix(numeric_list): recover coding context for bare follow-ups (#412)","url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/413"},{"body":"Fixes #16\n\n## Summary\n\nThis PR delivers the requirements from issue #16: every chat surface now answers in Russian, Hindi, and Chinese in addition to English; `What is X?` queries fall back to Wikipedia from the browser when the offline corpus does not cover the term; the deployable demo lives under `src/web/` next to the rest of the source tree; and the web UI persists every turn into an **append-only** memory log that can be exported and re-imported as Links Notation.\n\nA second pass (R97-R100, requested in the first reopen comment) makes the demo fully data-driven: multilingual responses, the concept table, and the tool registry are all loaded from seeded `.lino` files; the UI surfaces the tool catalog with a `thinking` vs `agent` mode badge; every reasoning step and tool invocation is recorded in the append-only log; and a single **Download bundle** action exports the seed + memory + environment metadata as one Links Notation document that the `Report issue` link references.\n\nA third pass (R101-R104, requested in the second reopen comment) generalises the seed loader so it is the canonical source for **every** interface — the Rust library, CLI, HTTP server, and Telegram webhook all `include_str!`-embed the same `data/seed/*.lino` files the browser worker fetches. The intent-routing rule book moves out of hardcoded match arms into `data/seed/intent-routing.lino` with explicit `keyword` / `phrase` / `token` / `combo` match semantics, and `seed::merged_bundle()` / `seed::parse_bundle()` (plus JS mirrors `FormalAiSeed.parseBundle` / `FormalAiSeed.loadFromBundle`) give the seed a complete single-file round-trip.\n\nA fourth pass (R105-R108, requested in the third reopen comment) makes `data/seed/` the **only** tracked seed tree, makes the seed **self-aware of every environment** it ships in, and lets a user **migrate their agent's memory between any pair of surfaces** with a single `.lino` file. Each new requirement is wired through the library so every CLI capability is reachable from Rust code as well.\n\n### Move `docs/demo/` → `src/web/`\n- Commit `765b2ea` relocates the deployable artefact so it sits next to the other library/CLI/web sources.\n- `.github/workflows/release.yml` GitHub Pages deploy job already points at `src/web`.\n\n### Multilingual surface (English, Russian, Hindi, Chinese)\n- Rust: `src/language.rs` detects the input language from Unicode blocks (Cyrillic, Devanagari, CJK), `src/engine.rs::language_aware_answer_for` returns localized greetings/identity/unknown, and `src/concepts.rs` adds ru/hi/zh aliases plus a `What is X?` prefix/suffix matcher for all four languages.\n- JS mirror: `src/web/formal_ai_worker.js` initialises mutable `MULTILINGUAL_ANSWERS`, `CONCEPTS`, and `TOOLS` tables from `data/seed/*.lino` (synced to `src/web/seed/` by `scripts/sync-seed.sh` and merged by `src/web/seed_loader.js`) instead of carrying hardcoded literals.\n\n### Wikipedia REST fallback (`What is X?`)\n- `src/web/formal_ai_worker.js` exposes `WIKIPEDIA_HOSTS`, `fetchWikipediaSummary`, and `tryWikipediaLookup`. The offline `CONCEPTS` table still wins whenever it can; the network call is reserved for out-of-corpus prompts.\n- The handler is intentionally last in the synchronous-handler chain and returns a structured answer with `source:` evidence so the user can audit the citation. Falls back to the English host when the detected language has no article.\n\n### Append-only memory log with export/import\n- `src/web/memory.js`: IndexedDB-backed store. Public API exposes `appendEvent`, `listEvents`, `importEvents`, `exportLinksNotation`, `parseLinksNotation`, `exportBundle`, `formatEvent` — and **no** `delete`/`deleteEvent`/`forget`/`clear`/`remove` operation. Append-only is enforced by *omission* of any code path that could remove records.\n- The event schema gains optional `kind`, `tool`, `inputs`, and `outputs` fields so reasoning steps and tool invocations can land in the same log without breaking older event shapes.\n- `src/web/app.js` topbar adds **Export memory**, **Import memory**, and **Download bundle** buttons plus a status indicator. Export downloads `formal-ai-memory.lino`; Import accepts the same shape and never deletes existing events; bundle downloads `formal-ai-bundle.lino`.\n\n### Data-driven configuration (R97-R100)\n- **Seeded constants.** `data/seed/multilingual-responses.lino`, `data/seed/concepts.lino` (with multilingual `aliases`), and `data/seed/tools.lino` define the agent's responses, concept table, and tool registry. The web worker loads them at boot via `src/web/seed_loader.js` and merges them into mutable runtime tables; user-provided changes are layered on top by editing the seed.\n- **Tool registry UI.** The context panel renders the loaded tools (`http_fetch`, `web_search`, `wikipedia_lookup`, `eval_js`, `read_local_file`, `append_memory`, `export_memory`) with a `thinking` vs `agent` mode badge. The worker dispatches `wikipedia_lookup`, `eval_js`, and `concept_lookup` end-to-end and records every invocation as a `kind:\"tool_call\"` event.\n- **Reasoning + tool-call events.** `solve()` returns structured `steps[]` (`impulse`, `formalize`, `detect_language`, `match_rule`/`dispatch_handler`/`invoke_tool`, `fallback`) and `toolCalls[]`. `appendAssistantMessage` writes each one to the append-only log alongside the user/assistant turns.\n- **Single-file reproducibility.** `FormalAiMemory.exportBundle({seed, events, info})` produces a `formal_ai_bundle` Links Notation document containing environment metadata, every seed file in full, and every recorded event. The prefilled **Report issue** body ends with an `Attach full state` section that asks the reporter to drag the bundle into the issue, so the maintainer can fully reconstruct the agent's state from a single attachment.\n\n### Universal seed + bundle round-trip (R101-R104)\n- **R101 — Universal seed loader.** `src/seed.rs` `include_str!`-embeds every `data/seed/*.lino` file and exposes typed accessors (`multilingual_responses_for`, `concept_records`, `tool_records`, `language_rule_records`, `prompt_pattern_records`, `intent_route_records`) plus `seed_files()` for the merged-bundle path. The Rust library, CLI binary, HTTP server, and Telegram webhook all read from these accessors so a single `data/seed/` edit reaches every surface; the browser worker continues to fetch the same files at runtime through `src/web/seed_loader.js`. `scripts/sync-seed.sh` keeps `src/web/seed/` mirrored from `data/seed/` for the GitHub Pages deploy.\n- **R102 — REQUIREMENTS colocation.** `REQUIREMENTS.md` now sits next to `VISION.md` at the repository root so the architecture story and the requirement matrix are reviewed together. All cross-references (case studies, changelog fragments not yet released) were updated.\n- **R103 — Intent routing as data.** `data/seed/intent-routing.lino` carries every routing rule with explicit match semantics: `keyword` (whole-prompt exact, case-insensitive), `phrase` (whole-prompt exact multi-word), `token` (single-token substring), and `combo` (all tokens present anywhere). The Rust handler dispatcher and the JS worker both parse this seed at boot and dispatch handlers from the data; previously hardcoded match arms are gone. A regression test (`hello_world_request_is_not_routed_to_greeting`) pins down the keyword/token split.\n- **R104 — Single-file bundle round-trip.** `seed::merged_bundle()` produces a `formal_ai_seed_bundle` Links Notation document containing every seed file in full; `seed::parse_bundle()` walks the document and recovers the per-category split files. The JS side mirrors this with `FormalAiSeed.parseBundle()` / `FormalAiSeed.loadFromBundle()`, so a single `.lino` upload reconstitutes the agent's static knowledge surface without sacrificing the maintenance-friendly split.\n\n### Self-aware environments + cross-surface memory migration (R105-R108)\n- **R105 — Single tracked seed tree.** `src/web/seed/` is now a generated deployment mirror (added to `.gitignore`); the tracked copies were deleted and `scripts/sync-seed.sh` is invoked from CI before the e2e job and the GitHub Pages upload so the browser still has the same `.lino` files at runtime. `data/seed/` is the only source of truth.\n- **R106 — Self-aware environments.** `data/seed/environments.lino` declares every interface the agent ships in (`browser`, `rust_library`, `cli`, `http_server`, `telegram`, `docker_microservice`) plus the cross-surface migration flows (`browser_to_cli`, `cli_to_browser`, `browser_to_browser`, `cli_to_cli`). `src/seed.rs` exposes typed accessors (`environment_directory`, `environment_records`, `EnvironmentRecord`, `MigrationFlow`) and the new `formal-ai environments` CLI command renders the directory so a user can list every surface and the documented portability flows from any one of them.\n- **R107 — Cross-surface memory migration.** `src/memory.rs` introduces a portable `MemoryStore` / `MemoryEvent` model that round-trips through the same `demo_memory` Links Notation format the browser writes to IndexedDB. `formal-ai memory export|import|show` and `formal-ai bundle export|import` give the CLI parity with the browser's `Export memory` / `Import memory` / `Download bundle` buttons, and `--path -` selects stdin/stdout so `formal-ai memory export --from … --path - | ssh host formal-ai memory import --path -` works without temp files. Library users get the same capability via `export_memory_links_notation`, `parse_memory_links_notation`, `export_memory_bundle`, and `extract_memory_from_bundle`.\n- **R108 — Library-first availability.** Every CLI capability is also re-exported from `src/lib.rs` (engine, protocol, seed accessors, environment directory, memory primitives), so a downstream Rust crate can embed `formal-ai` and reach the same answers, the same intent routes, the same environment directory, and the same import/export pipeline without shelling out to the binary. A new `environment_records_match_directory` test pins library/CLI parity.\n\n### Playwright e2e (local + GitHub Pages)\n- `tests/e2e/tests/multilingual.spec.js` — 14 tests covering:\n  - Russian/Hindi greetings replying in the same language\n  - Chinese identity prompt (`你是谁?`) replying in Chinese\n  - Russian/Chinese `What is X?` resolving from the offline `CONCEPTS` table\n  - Wikipedia REST fallback for `What is Albert Einstein?` (stubbed via `page.route` so the test is hermetic)\n  - Export/Import buttons present + producing a `.lino` file with `demo_memory`/`role`/`content`\n  - Assertion that `window.FormalAiMemory` exposes no delete/forget/clear API\n  - `Download bundle` produces a `formal_ai_bundle` file with seed and memory log\n  - `Report issue` link references the bundle in the prefilled body\n  - Tool registry surfaces seed-loaded tools with mode badges\n  - Reasoning steps and tool calls land in the append-only log\n- Both `tests/e2e/playwright.local.config.js` (PR runs against `npx serve src/web` after `scripts/sync-seed.sh`) and `tests/e2e/playwright.pages.config.js` (post-deploy run against the live `link-assistant.github.io/formal-ai`) match `**/multilingual.spec.js`.\n\n### Documentation\n- `REQUIREMENTS.md` (relocated from `docs/REQUIREMENTS.md`) now covers R90-R108 — including R105 (`data/seed/` as single source of truth), R106 (self-aware environments via `environments.lino`), R107 (`formal-ai memory` / `formal-ai bundle` round-trip with `formal_ai_bundle`), and R108 (library-first parity).\n- `VISION.md` adds the **Self-Aware Environments** and **Library-First Availability** pillars, names `data/seed/environments.lino` and the migration flows, and points to `MemoryStore` / `export_memory_bundle` as the cross-surface portability primitives.\n- `docs/case-studies/issue-16/README.md`: full case study with raw GitHub data, online research, requirements-to-implementation mapping, architecture notes, the \"Follow-Up: Universal Seed and Single-File Round-Trip (PR #17 reopen 2)\" section for R101-R104, and the new \"Follow-Up: Self-Aware Environments and Cross-Surface Memory Migration (PR #17 reopen 3)\" section for R105-R108.\n- A `docs_requirements::issue_16_followup_documents_capture_universal_seed_and_memory_migration` test pins the required strings across REQUIREMENTS.md / VISION.md / case study so the requirement matrix, vision narrative, and case study cannot silently drift apart.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cargo fmt --all -- --check` ✓\n- `cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings` ✓\n- `cargo test --all-targets` — 56 lib + 7 integration + 156 active unit tests passing, 69 MVP-target tests ignored, 0 failed ✓\n- `cd tests/e2e && npx playwright test --config=playwright.local.config.js` — 33 tests pass (19 existing demo + 14 multilingual/Wikipedia/memory/bundle/tool-registry/reasoning) ✓\n\n## Requirements Coverage\n\n| ID | Requirement | Where |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| R90 | Move deployable demo to `src/web/` | commit `765b2ea` + `.github/workflows/release.yml` |\n| R91 | Multilingual greetings / identity / unknown / concept lookup (ru/hi/zh) | `src/language.rs`, `src/engine.rs`, `src/concepts.rs`, `src/web/formal_ai_worker.js` |\n| R92 | `What is X?` via Wikipedia from the browser | `src/web/formal_ai_worker.js` (`tryWikipediaLookup`) |\n| R93 | Playwright e2e locally + against live deploy | `tests/e2e/tests/multilingual.spec.js`, both `playwright.local.config.js` and `playwright.pages.config.js` |\n| R94 | Export/Import full memory as Links Notation | `src/web/memory.js`, `src/web/app.js` topbar |\n| R95 | Append-only by default; no delete/forget API | `src/web/memory.js` (deliberately no delete path); pinned by an e2e test |\n| R96 | Case study under `docs/case-studies/issue-16/` | `README.md` + `raw-data/` |\n| R97 | Externalize hardcoded constants to seeded `.lino` | `data/seed/*.lino` + `src/web/seed/` + `src/web/seed_loader.js` |\n| R98 | Render seeded tool registry with mode badges | `src/web/app.js` `[data-testid=\"tool-registry\"]` + `src/web/styles.css` |\n| R99 | Record reasoning + tool invocations in append-only memory | `src/web/formal_ai_worker.js` `steps[]`/`toolCalls[]` + `src/web/app.js` `appendAssistantMessage` + `src/web/memory.js` schema |\n| R100 | Single `Download bundle` + Report-issue linkage | `FormalAiMemory.exportBundle` + topbar button + prefilled issue body |\n| R101 | `data/seed/` canonical across every interface | `src/seed.rs` (`include_str!` for Rust/CLI/server/Telegram) + `src/web/seed_loader.js` (browser) |\n| R102 | `REQUIREMENTS.md` colocated with `VISION.md` | repository root |\n| R103 | Intent routing as data with explicit match semantics | `data/seed/intent-routing.lino` + dispatcher in `src/solver_helpers.rs` + JS worker |\n| R104 | Single-file bundle round-trip | `seed::merged_bundle()` / `seed::parse_bundle()` + `FormalAiSeed.parseBundle` / `FormalAiSeed.loadFromBundle` |\n| R105 | `data/seed/` as the only tracked seed tree | `.gitignore` (mirror is generated), `scripts/sync-seed.sh`, `.github/workflows/release.yml` |\n| R106 | Self-aware environments + migration flows | `data/seed/environments.lino` + `seed::environment_directory()` + `formal-ai environments` CLI |\n| R107 | Cross-surface memory migration via a single `.lino` | `src/memory.rs` (`MemoryStore`, `MemoryEvent`, `export_bundle`, `extract_memory_from_bundle`) + `formal-ai memory` / `formal-ai bundle` CLI |\n| R108 | Library-first parity for every CLI capability | `src/lib.rs` re-exports of every public surface + library-parity tests in `tests/unit/formal_ai.rs` |\n","headRefName":"issue-16-f76f85f72657","mergedAt":"2026-05-15T12:20:10Z","number":17,"title":"Multilingual chat (ru/hi/zh), Wikipedia fallback, append-only memory, data-driven agent","url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/17"}]
