| RC1: one-source answers | PR #795's predecessor selected one preferred URL and retained only the latest fetch, structurally losing triangulation and URL identity. | `docs/case-studies/issue-781/raw-data/reproduction-before-fix.log` | PR #795 stores bounded per-URL fetch records and renders each citation; `compatibility_research_fetches_and_cites_independent_sources`. |
| RC2: silent/batched actions | Tool responses were serialized with no assistant text, and all pending fetches could be emitted together. Clients either showed only a spinner/tool name or waited on a multi-action turn. | `../reproduction-protocol-surfaces-before-fix.log`, screenshot `../github/issue-comment-5016917806-stuck.png` | `tool_action_narration` is emitted before calls on all protocols; web research schedules one fetch per turn. `../reproduction-after-core-fix.log`. |
